cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Crisis Baseline Kit or its baseline data in your work,
  please cite it. Baseline data should also credit its upstream sources
  (WorldPop, OCHA COD-AB) as recorded in each bundle's manifest.json.
title: Crisis Baseline Kit
type: software
authors:
  - alias: alfredshingai
repository-code: "https://github.com/alfredshingai/crisis-baseline-kit"
url: "https://github.com/alfredshingai/crisis-baseline-kit/releases"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pre-crisis baseline maps and databases built from public
  data. One command builds a documented, quality-gated baseline for a
  country: administrative boundaries with p-codes (OCHA COD-AB),
  population rasters (WorldPop) and per-district zonal statistics,
  packaged with full provenance (source URLs, licenses, versions,
  checksums) and a bundled map viewer. Pilot country: Malawi.
keywords:
  - humanitarian
  - GIS
  - open-data
  - disaster-response
  - preparedness
  - baseline
license: MIT
